HST Office packaging: Debian Maintainer and system library dependencies.

EPM writes the packinfo "vendor" into the Maintainer field of every .deb;
upstream hard-codes "The Document Foundation". Replace it with the HST Office
vendor (HASON TECH, matching --with-vendor). The copyright line is left
unchanged on purpose: the code remains copyrighted by its upstream authors.

The brand package (the package every other HST package ultimately depends on)
also declares the system libraries soffice needs, so `apt install ./*.deb`
produces a launchable suite on a clean Ubuntu 24.04. The list was computed
with dpkg-shlibdeps over every ELF file of the installed tree plus python3
for the system-Python UNO bridge (names are the 24.04 t64 package names).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
